  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Tunnel rescue",
  "description": "Everyone runs around inside a box holding a ball in their hands. One or two taggers (red), depending on group size, try to tag the others. Anyone who is tagged stands with legs apart to make a tunnel.\n\nA teammate rescues you by putting their ball down, passing it with their foot through your tunnel and then crawling through after it. Change taggers often. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass with the inside of the foot – calm and accurate so the ball goes through the tunnel."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Look for teammates who need help."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Taggers: work together and chase towards the corners."
    }
  ],
